course: dictionary
lesson: 7659
title: Pronouns: little words that stand in for nouns
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pronoun is a little word that takes the place of a noun, so we do not have to keep repeating names. Instead of «Sam lost Sam's bag, so Sam looked for Sam's bag», we say «Sam lost his bag, so he looked for it». The words he and it are pronouns.
explain: Pronouns have two forms. Subject forms do the action: I, he, she, we, they. Object forms receive the action: me, him, her, us, them. So we say «Sam and I went», but «Mum gave sweets to Ben and me».
explain: A pronoun must be clear. «Tom met Sam and he laughed» does not tell us who laughed. The noun a pronoun points back to is called its antecedent, so always ask: which noun does this pronoun stand for?
explain: Some people ask others to use particular pronouns for them, such as she/her or they/them. It is kind to use the pronouns people ask for.
fact: A pronoun is a word used instead of a noun.
fact: Personal pronouns include I, you, he, she, it, we and they, and their object forms me, him, her, us and them.
fact: Possessive pronouns show who something belongs to: «mine», «yours», «hers», «ours» and «theirs».
fact: Relative pronouns like «who», «which» and «that» join extra information to a noun: «the girl who won».
fact: Little words like «my», «your» and «his» before a noun are possessive determiners, while «mine» and «yours» standing alone are pronouns.
exercise: Which word in «Mum gave sweets to Ben and me» is a pronoun? | Mum | sweets | *me | Ben
exercise: Which pronoun is unclear in «Tom met Sam and he laughed»? | laughed | Tom | *he | Sam
exercise: Which word in «That bike is mine» is a possessive pronoun? | is | bike | that | *mine
test: Which word is a relative pronoun in «the girl who won»? | girl | *who | the | won
test: Choose the right word: «Sam and ___ went home.» | mine | us | me | *I
exam: In «Your bag is here, and mine is over there», which word is a possessive determiner rather than a pronoun? | mine | *Your | here | over
